# CFF 1.2.0 offers only the "software" and "dataset" types; "software" is used for this documentation repository.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this research, please cite it as below."
title: "Ouroboros: research toward a lifelong, model-independent artificial mind (Research Preview 0.1)"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-preview"
authors:
  - given-names: "Christopher"
    family-names: "Ayers"
abstract: >-
  Ouroboros is a research program exploring whether one persistent artificial
  intelligence can grow throughout its lifetime, become measurably more capable
  from verified experience, and preserve the same evolving mind while its
  underlying AI models are upgraded or replaced. Model independence and
  lifelong operation are research goals and have not been demonstrated. This
  repository is the public research record: thesis, conceptual architecture,
  roadmap, experiment ledger and results. It contains no implementation.
keywords:
  - artificial-intelligence
  - continual-learning
  - lifelong-learning
  - self-improving-ai
  - ai-agents
  - metacognition
